Subject: [PATCH] [ADT] Drop the non-null static_assert in bind_front/bind_back

The compile-time-callable overloads of llvm::bind_front and llvm::bind_back
sanity-check their non-type template parameter with:

    if constexpr (std::is_pointer_v<decltype(ConstFn)> ||
                  std::is_member_pointer_v<decltype(ConstFn)>)
      static_assert(ConstFn != nullptr);

Wolfi's gcc is built with -fno-delete-null-pointer-checks enabled by default
as a hardening measure. Under that flag GCC will not constant-fold the address
of a function template instantiation compared against null, so the assertion's
condition is no longer a constant expression and the build fails:

llvm/include/llvm/ADT/STLForwardCompat.h:334:27: error: '(llvm::PatternMatch::match<const llvm::Value, ...> != 0)' is not a constant expression
  334 |     static_assert(ConstFn != nullptr);
llvm/include/llvm/ADT/STLForwardCompat.h:334:27: error: non-constant condition for static assertion

This first bites in lib/Transforms/Vectorize/SLPVectorizer.cpp, which reaches
it via PatternMatch::match_fn(). LLVM 23 rewrote match_fn() to use
bind_back<match<Val, Pattern>>(); in LLVM 22 it returned a hand-written
MatchFunctor and so was unaffected.

Drop the assertion rather than re-enabling -fdelete-null-pointer-checks for
the whole LLVM build, which would give up the hardening for every translation
unit to satisfy one sanity check. The check only rejects an explicitly-null
callable, which no in-tree caller passes, and a null ConstFn would in any case
fail at the point of call.

Origin: vendor
Bug: https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/202062
Bug-GCC: https://gcc.gnu.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=97913

---
 llvm/include/llvm/ADT/STLForwardCompat.h | 8 --------
 1 file changed, 8 deletions(-)

--- a/llvm/include/llvm/ADT/STLForwardCompat.h
+++ b/llvm/include/llvm/ADT/STLForwardCompat.h
@@ -300,10 +300,6 @@
 template <auto ConstFn, typename... BindArgsT>
 constexpr auto
 bind_front(BindArgsT &&...BindArgs) { // NOLINT(readability-identifier-naming)
-  if constexpr (std::is_pointer_v<decltype(ConstFn)> ||
-                std::is_member_pointer_v<decltype(ConstFn)>)
-    static_assert(ConstFn != nullptr);
-
   return detail::BindStorage<
       /*BindFront=*/true, std::tuple<std::decay_t<BindArgsT>...>,
       detail::FnConstant<ConstFn>, std::index_sequence_for<BindArgsT...>>(
@@ -329,10 +325,6 @@
 template <auto ConstFn, typename... BindArgsT>
 constexpr auto
 bind_back(BindArgsT &&...BindArgs) { // NOLINT(readability-identifier-naming)
-  if constexpr (std::is_pointer_v<decltype(ConstFn)> ||
-                std::is_member_pointer_v<decltype(ConstFn)>)
-    static_assert(ConstFn != nullptr);
-
   return detail::BindStorage<
       /*BindFront=*/false, std::tuple<std::decay_t<BindArgsT>...>,
       detail::FnConstant<ConstFn>, std::index_sequence_for<BindArgsT...>>(
